---
title: What each model means by a forecast day
---
%% FEWS4All - the forecast timeline, as a 16-column day grid.
%% A SOLID block names the days it covers, so it earns those days a place on the
%% timeline. A DASHED block covers days without naming any: it is drawn on each
%% of them, but cannot by itself make a day worth stepping to.
%% One colour per model across every figure: GEOGLOWS orange (the same orange
%% the application uses), Flood Hub blue, GloFAS green. On the map itself they
%% share a palette and are told apart by the side panel, so this key belongs to
%% the documentation, not the app.
%% Edit the :N span after a block to move it; the spans in each row total 16.
%% Render:  reporting/regenerate.sh timeline
%% By hand, from this folder, to where the manual looks for it:
%%   mmdc -i forecast-timeline.mmd -o ../build/figures/forecast-timeline.pdf -b white --pdfFit
%% Without mmdc, swap "mmdc" for "npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli".
%% --pdfFit trims the page to the diagram. Output is vector, so it stays sharp
%% at any size; for a PNG instead, swap the extension and add -s 4 (a scale
%% factor -- mermaid sizes the canvas to the diagram and ignores -w).
%% The widest cell in any row sets how wide the whole diagram is, so keep the
%% long explanatory text in the caption, not in a block.
%% NOTE one Mermaid quirk: a bare "%%" line is a parse error in block diagrams.
%% Every comment line here must carry text after the percent signs.
block-beta
  columns 16

  axis["Forecast day - one column per day, 0 is today"]:16

  d0["0"] d1["1"] d2["2"] d3["3"] d4["4"] d5["5"] d6["6"] d7["7"]
  d8["8"] d9["9"] d10["10"] d11["11"] d12["12"] d13["13"] d14["14"] d15["15"]

  geo["GEOGLOWS - one 06:00 UTC step per day, days 0-9"]:10
  geox["nothing past day 9"]:6

  gf1["GloFAS 1-3<br/>published as 0-3"]:4
  gf2["GloFAS 4-10"]:7
  gf3["GloFAS 11-15"]:5

  space:5
  fhw["Flood Hub<br/>window"]:2
  fhnote["window depends on gauge"]:9

  fhspan["Flood Hub gauge with no published window - covers every day, names none"]:16

  flash["Flash<br/>24 h"]:2
  flashx["flash floods never reach beyond tomorrow"]:14

  classDef axis fill:#F8FAFC,stroke:#CBD5E1,color:#475569
  classDef axislab fill:#FFFFFF,stroke:#FFFFFF,color:#475569
  classDef geoc fill:#FFEDD5,stroke:#EA580C,color:#7C2D12
  classDef gloc fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#15803D,color:#14532D
  classDef fhc fill:#DBEAFE,stroke:#2563EB,color:#1E3A8A
  classDef flsc fill:#FEE2E2,stroke:#DC2626,color:#7F1D1D
  classDef ghost fill:#FFFFFF,stroke:#CBD5E1,color:#64748B,stroke-dasharray:3 3
  classDef span fill:#F5F8FF,stroke:#2563EB,color:#1E3A8A,stroke-dasharray:5 4

  class d0,d1,d2,d3,d4,d5,d6,d7,d8,d9,d10,d11,d12,d13,d14,d15 axis
  class axis axislab
  class geo geoc
  class gf1,gf2,gf3 gloc
  class fhw fhc
  class flash flsc
  class geox,flashx,fhnote ghost
  class fhspan span
